# Bhavya OS — Code Owners
#
# Existing baseline: a single owner holds default review on every path.
# The entries below make the permanent platform contract and its enforcement
# explicitly owned, so a change to the rules cannot silently land alongside the
# code it governs.
#
# Precedence follows AGENTS.md §1: constitution > AGENTS.md > CONTEXT.md chain >
# architecture truth > contracts/standards > skills > implementation.
# Where two authorities conflict and precedence does not resolve it, stop for a
# human. Do not silently rewrite either authority.

# Default owner for everything not listed below.
* @manohar-lal

# --- Permanent operating contract -------------------------------------------
# Changes here alter the rules every agent and workflow is bound by.
# Requires human review: an agent may not relax these unilaterally.
/AGENTS.md                                   @manohar-lal
/docs/architecture/PLATFORM-TRUTH.md        @manohar-lal
/CODEOWNERS                                  @manohar-lal
/.github/pull_request_template.md           @manohar-lal

# Contract enforcement. Changing the checker without changing the contract
# (or vice versa) is how enforcement quietly stops matching policy.
/scripts/validate-platform-contract.mjs     @manohar-lal

# --- Deployment ------------------------------------------------------------
# Production deployment, secrets and targets. Merge to master deploys.
/.github/workflows/deploy-cloudflare.yml    @manohar-lal
/apps/ai-institute/wrangler.json            @manohar-lal
/apps/ai-institute/next.config.mjs          @manohar-lal

# --- Agent instructions -----------------------------------------------------
# Project-owned skills and agent configuration.
/.opencode/skills/                           @manohar-lal
/.opencode/command/                          @manohar-lal
/opencode.json                              @manohar-lal

# --- Security and data boundaries ------------------------------------------
# Auth, database, storage credentials. Privileged material stays server-side.
/packages/auth/                             @manohar-lal
/packages/database/                         @manohar-lal
/packages/security/                         @manohar-lal
/apps/ai-institute/src/lib/b2/              @manohar-lal
/apps/ai-institute/src/lib/auth/            @manohar-lal

# --- Design authority -------------------------------------------------------
# Tokens and canonical components: no hardcoded values, no duplicate systems.
/packages/platform-ui/src/styles/            @manohar-lal
/packages/platform-ui/src/components/       @manohar-lal
/docs/constitution/                         @manohar-lal